    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0471" n="431" xml:id="pg431"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1483.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 24, 1865</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With a view to such proceedings on your
                    part as may tend to prevent any political intervention by Great Britain in the
                    affairs of the Hawaiian kingdom prejudicial to the interests of the United
                    States or its citizens resident in that kingdom, I enclose a copy of a letter of
                    the 27th ultimo, addressed by Mr. R. Anderson, of Boston, to the Hon. Charles
                    Sumner.</p>
                <p>I will thank you promptly to communicate to this department any information in
                    regard to the relations between Great Britain and the Sandwich Islands which may
                    come to your knowledge.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d290-a1.xml" xpointer="d290-a1"/>
            </div>
